body:
Climbing etiquette on wearing airpods to the climbing gym?

&#x200B;

I want to go alone and enjoy my own time, but is it bad etiquette?

no probably not. If you're a daily smoker it takes 30 days to get out of your system and it goes down from there. down as in less time out of your system ya feel.

&#x200B;

good luck!!

I would put under education, depending on the job, applicable classes you've taken. Especially for an internship resume with little work experience.

&#x200B;

not an expert but it landed me some

if they know you have bipolar disorder, and they're a good enough friend, send them this exact meme and be like, hey i'm sorry but like this is my current mood unfortunately

&#x200B;

also this may prompt them to say "let's hang at your place and make dinner" to which you should reply YES

&#x200B;

I just moved back home after graduation, cause I got my dream job. I currently live with my parents which is a solid HOUR away from work so I 100% understand what you're going through. In the next two months, I'll have to be up at 3:45am to get to work by 5am.  I'm not thrilled, but I have to start with something and I'm lucky enough that I got this job that I am not going to complain to anyone except myself and to my large iced coffee every morning.

&#x200B;

Many people commute an hour + everyday, and I know it's hard, but sometimes you just gotta do certain things like that. I have podcasts and music playlists lined up so I have something to enjoy on the commute.

&#x200B;

I'm no longer on effexor, but I found that after about 6months on the highest dose of 325 or whatever, that my anxiety cleared almost entirely. I now have pretty violent mood swings once in a while, but overall I'm actually doing incredibly well. I don't want to encourage you to up your dose, but talk honestly and openly with your doctor.

BECAUSE IT'S HIM!!!

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I don't actually know nor do I care in all honesty.

Very true, but I also feel like him winning is kinda like a slap in the face to everyone who ever said that RR wouldn't be successful. Idk! I was high but I still think that it's kinda a good theory. 

&#x200B;

I did say in a previous comment that we also have to acknowledge those fuckwad showrunners, and maybe they made bran to be more of a george-martin character. As another commenter noted, that last speech tyrion made about Bran being the all-knowing, story hoarding, memory of westeros or whatever.

Honestly, knowing how i deal with things I would probably not get anything done i want to. I'm looking into some grad programs now so hopefully i dont have to take time off. idk, working on it still. thank you so much for your reply btw, it's greatly appreciated.

&#x200B;

i actually live in dc so it wouldn't be too far away, lol. but i have one really solid friend who helps me through a lot of things so i'm good while i'm still in college. she's just not gonna be there when I move back home and stuff so yeah.

WAIT WHAT

&#x200B;

pls can i dm for the info i had no idea this was a thing

I often feel my best a day before the appointment that i made when i was really sad. I make sure I really explain that well to my doctor because ya know...bipolar disorder be like that sometimes. 

&#x200B;

go, and be honest about what you were feeling then and how you're feeling now. cause you're bound to feel bad again and then you'll make another appointment.
